WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.350
Fieldnote seven.

2
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.120
Things that are not true.

3
00:00:09.194 --> 00:00:12.444
Which reasonable assumptions
will cost me an afternoon?

4
00:00:13.852 --> 00:00:15.702
The assumptions that cause trouble.

5
00:00:16.092 --> 00:00:20.262
Each is a reasonable thing to believe
about a Kubernetes and Azure system.

6
00:00:20.572 --> 00:00:23.372
The project's own
documentation says otherwise,

7
00:00:23.372 --> 00:00:24.902
and names how to check.

8
00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:29.538
The smoke test passed, so the API works.

9
00:00:29.688 --> 00:00:34.408
Not quite. The scheduled smoke
test defaults to the bare profile,

10
00:00:34.408 --> 00:00:37.298
which deploys no OSDU services at all.

11
00:00:37.688 --> 00:00:40.808
It proves infrastructure
and GitOps readiness,

12
00:00:40.808 --> 00:00:43.458
not authenticated API behavior.

13
00:00:44.008 --> 00:00:48.258
Ask yourself, and read
the run's profile input.

14
00:00:50.292 --> 00:00:52.782
Re-applying the manifest will retry it.

15
00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:56.462
A HelmRelease that has used
up its retries is stalled,

16
00:00:56.532 --> 00:01:00.222
and re-applying the unchanged
manifest does not move it.

17
00:01:00.612 --> 00:01:04.612
spi reconcile clears the
count and forces one attempt;

18
00:01:04.612 --> 00:01:06.862
a bad chart needs a real change.

19
00:01:07.412 --> 00:01:08.622
Ask Flux.

20
00:01:10.688 --> 00:01:12.218
The role assignment is missing.

21
00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:17.008
Maybe not. Cosmos DB data-plane
grants are Cosmos-native,

22
00:01:17.008 --> 00:01:20.538
and they do not appear in standard
Azure role-assignment queries.

23
00:01:20.688 --> 00:01:24.538
Propagation can lag, and services
cache clients at startup.

24
00:01:25.328 --> 00:01:29.818
Ask the CLI and Bicep, and
list the Cosmos assignments.

25
00:01:31.836 --> 00:01:34.886
There is a certificate, so
the connection is encrypted.

26
00:01:35.676 --> 00:01:40.646
Port 80 still serves the API
routes, and nothing redirects.

27
00:01:41.116 --> 00:01:46.566
A client that uses an http address
sends its bearer token in plain text.

28
00:01:46.956 --> 00:01:51.286
Ask Flux, and use the https endpoint.

29
00:01:53.336 --> 00:01:56.386
The teardown job was
green, so it was deleted.

30
00:01:56.536 --> 00:01:58.946
Green means the deletion was requested.

31
00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:04.066
The step tolerates failure, which is
why a separate orphan sweeper exists.

32
00:02:04.376 --> 00:02:08.546
Ask the CLI and Bicep, and
check that the group is gone.

33
00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:14.686
Template sync will overwrite the
workflow change I made in my fork.

34
00:02:14.916 --> 00:02:17.006
It opens a pull request instead.

35
00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:21.886
Sync Template proposes the
difference as one pull request,

36
00:02:21.956 --> 00:02:24.046
labeled template sync.

37
00:02:24.756 --> 00:02:27.716
A change you want to keep
is a review comment,

38
00:02:27.716 --> 00:02:29.166
not a lost file.

39
00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:31.486
Ask the service fork.

40
00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:36.490
The restore step puts
the previous image back.

41
00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.130
Only while this run still owns the pin.

42
00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:44.560
If a newer run has pinned the slot,
the reset leaves it alone and exits 2.

43
00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.650
A cancelled run strands its pin
until an operator clears it.

44
00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:52.090
Ask yourself, and read the lock's pins.

45
00:02:54.324 --> 00:02:55.534
So now you can say:

46
00:02:55.764 --> 00:02:59.604
when something looks wrong,
I know which owner to ask,

47
00:02:59.604 --> 00:03:02.094
and which command shows
its view of the world.

48
00:03:02.404 --> 00:03:07.534
Provisioning, convergence, readiness,
and proof are different signals,

49
00:03:07.604 --> 00:03:10.094
and I check the one I actually need.

50
00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:15.814
That is the path, from the
resource group to the seam.

51
00:03:16.204 --> 00:03:19.254
Each check names the lesson
where its idea was built.

52
00:03:19.564 --> 00:03:21.414
Go back to it when you need it.

